.nh
.TH "PB-CONFIG-SET" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-config-set - Set a local configuration value


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb config set <key> <value> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Set one local configuration key of this CLI installation. The keys are server (the
Paperboat server URL: absolute http or https, without credentials, query or fragment) and
ssh-target-port (1-65535, the port registered for this machine's managed SSH target). Check the
effective value afterwards with pb config show; pb config unset server removes the setting.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for set

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb config set server https://api.example.test
  pb config set ssh-target-port 2222
  pb config set server https://api.example.test --json
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-config(1)\fP
